        'Your iron and haemoglobin levels are commonly rechecked in the second half of pregnancy, often alongside your glucose test, since your body\'s iron needs rise further as your blood volume expands and your baby builds their own iron stores. Anemia is genuinely common in Indian pregnancies, so this recheck is routine, not a sign of a specific concern.',
