        'Your blood volume keeps increasing through pregnancy, and your baby draws on your iron supply to build their own reserves for after birth, both of which mean your iron needs keep climbing even if your levels looked fine earlier on. India has notably high rates of anemia in pregnancy, which is exactly why this ongoing monitoring, rather than a single early check, matters so much here.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
