    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Fundal height is the distance, in centimetres, from your pubic bone to the top of your womb, and it\'s a simple way for your doctor to track your baby\'s growth at every visit. From around now, it roughly matches your week of pregnancy, so 24 weeks often measures close to 24 centimetres.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'This measurement gives a quick, no-equipment way to check that growth is roughly on track between your scheduled scans, without needing an ultrasound at every single visit. It\'s not perfectly precise, since your body type and your baby\'s position can shift the number slightly, which is exactly why it\'s used as a general trend check rather than an exact measurement.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If your fundal height measures notably larger or smaller than expected for your week, your doctor may simply keep a closer eye on the trend over your next few visits, or occasionally suggest a growth scan for more detail. A single measurement slightly off the expected number rarely means anything on its own.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor what your fundal height measurement was and whether it\'s tracking as expected for your week.',
