    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Yes, to some degree. Regular activity and a balanced diet earlier in pregnancy, ideally started even before conception if possible, can meaningfully lower your chance of developing gestational diabetes, though it can\'t eliminate risk entirely for everyone.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'A landmark Finnish study found that starting diet and exercise changes before 20 weeks reduced gestational diabetes cases by around 39 percent in women already at higher risk. An ongoing Indian study, based in Vellore, is specifically testing whether daily yoghurt and walking can meaningfully lower risk for Indian women, reflecting genuine research interest in accessible, low-cost prevention here.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'If you know you have risk factors, family history, previous gestational diabetes, PCOS, or being above a healthy weight range, talk to your doctor early about starting sensible activity and dietary habits well before your screening window. This isn\'t about guaranteeing you\'ll avoid a diagnosis; it\'s about giving yourself a genuinely better chance.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor about your personal risk factors and whether earlier lifestyle changes or earlier screening make sense for you.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
