    month: 6,
    question: 'What if I struggle with the glucose drink, or feel nauseous during the test?',
    category: 'Scans & Appointments',
    applicability: 'Month 6 (weeks 23-27)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Mild nausea or dizziness during or after the glucose drink is common and not a sign anything is wrong with you or your baby. A few simple tricks genuinely help: ask for the drink chilled, sip it steadily rather than gulping, and sit quietly afterward rather than moving around.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'The drink is quite concentrated and very sweet, closer to flat soda than anything you\'d normally drink quickly, which is exactly why it can unsettle your stomach, especially in pregnancy when nausea is already more easily triggered. This is a known, common reaction to the drink itself, not a reflection of your blood sugar or your baby\'s wellbeing.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Ask if the drink can be refrigerated beforehand, since cold is generally easier to tolerate than room temperature. Sipping through a straw, or briefly pinching your nose while drinking, can reduce how strong the taste feels. Sit calmly afterward, ideally with a book or something to distract you, and avoid sudden movement, which tends to make nausea worse. If you actually vomit shortly after drinking it, tell the staff immediately, since the test will likely need to be rescheduled rather than counted as done.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Mention a strong fear of nausea to your doctor beforehand; they may have specific suggestions for your particular test protocol.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'This test has a bit of a reputation, and for good reason, but a few small tricks make it a genuinely manageable, one-time discomfort rather than something to dread.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Mild nausea or dizziness during the test is common and harmless.',
        'Ask for the drink chilled; cold is easier to tolerate.',
        'Sip steadily through a straw, or pinch your nose while drinking.',
        'Sit calmly afterward and avoid sudden movement.',
        'Tell staff immediately if you vomit; the test may need rescheduling.',
      ]),
    ],
